=================== MEMORY ===================

Nothing here allocates. The partials arm holds eight `__m128i` accumulators and
a `[[i32; 15]; 8]` on the stack, exactly as the scalar and NEON arms already
did; no heap traffic and no buffer size changed.

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED: that x86 had no vector arm for `cdef_find_dir` before this; the
frame and per-kernel Ir on two contents at p6 and one at p2; the per-block cost
against C's dual kernel; the wall clock on four cells at 21 paired rounds each
with a matched same-binary control on a verifiably quiet box, and that the one
apparently-negative cell does not reproduce; that every arm equals real C under
a forced token sweep and equals the scalar core across the bail-out boundary.

NOT ESTABLISHED: that this closes the direction search — it is still 7.46x C's
instructions, and HALF of that is defect (b) above, the apply recomputing what
the search already cached, which no kernel change can touch. Also unmeasured:
p10, any qp but 40, 10-bit, and the inter arm. The residual per block (776 vs
C's 208) is not decomposed between the vector partials and the shared scalar
cost/argmax tail (`cdef_dir_from_partials`), which is common to all three arms
and is the obvious next thing to measure before optimising further.
